{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n5 of the 9 local `make verify` logs of Nov 19-20 2026 ran inside the Claude Code agent sandbox (their pytest temp dirs sit under `/private/tmp/claude-502`, the sandbox TMPDIR, and pip reports the sandbox proxy's `Tunnel connection failed: 403 not in this command's allowed_domains`). Those 5 runs each failed 37 to 45 tests that pass in CI. The 5 complete unsandboxed runs of the same days (temp dirs under `/var/folders`) failed only the then-red `test_resign_makes_enforced_verify_pass_with_era_keys` (fixed by 2825b4fe283) and, once, the review-bot 3 s marker tracked in stinky-blushing-gelding.\n\n## Verified cause\nA controlled A/B on Nov 20 2026 ran one fixed set of 21 test modules (origin/main 8e1d15e664f, `-n 4`, same host, minutes apart, load average 17-21; logs `ab-sandboxed.log` / `ab-unsandboxed.log` under `.rebar/scratch/s05f74084-f2/` in worktree f2-verify-parity). Outside the sandbox all 379 tests passed in 187.58 s. Inside, 18 failed and 3 errored (655.42 s). Every failure traces to 2 capabilities the sandbox denies, each reproduced directly in a sandboxed shell:\n- AF_UNIX sockets. `socket(AF_UNIX).bind()` in the temp dir raises `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted`. Breaks all 9 tests in `tests/unit/test_reclaim_resign.py` (their private `ssh-agent -a <sock>` never binds, so `ssh-add` fails with \"Error connecting to agent: No such file or directory\") and both tests in `tests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py`.\n- Outbound HTTPS to 2 hosts:\n  - `semgrep.dev`. The opengrep/semgrep backend pre-validates each detector with `semgrep --validate`, which downloads the `p/semgrep-rule-lints` ruleset from `semgrep.dev`. In the sandbox that request is denied (`deny network-outbound semgrep.dev:443`), so validation retries for about 60 s and the harness abstains. This fails 4 tests in `tests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py` / `test_code_review_public_exposure.py` (their negative tests pass falsely after 122 s each) and 2 in `tests/unit/grounding/test_conformance.py`. The existing `configure_semgrep_settings_file` redirect in `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py` (ticket 985f-0ec5) does work: with it, `semgrep scan` succeeds inside the sandbox (measured); only `--validate` fails, on the network.\n  - `pypi.org`. Isolated builds (`python -m build`) cannot fetch `hatchling` (`deny network-outbound pypi.org:443`): the 3 `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py` errors and `tests/unit/test_attestation_signing.py::test_hook_falls_back_to_git_when_env_unset`.\nThese are not test defects: the suite legitimately exercises an ssh-agent socket, the network guard's AF_UNIX allowance, a validated real detector, and a real isolated build, and CI hosts provide all of them. A per-test shim cannot cover them, because the denied capability is the operation under test.\n\n## Approach\nMake the requirement explicit and enforced instead of producing a misleading red (or a false green) after a 25-minute run: `make verify` refuses up front on a host that lacks one of these capabilities, and says which.\n- New `scripts/check_verify_host.py` (marked `# mechanism-ok: ci_gate scripts/check_verify_host.py — d492-04db-b79e-428f`). Three probes, each a function returning `(ok, detail)` and taking its I/O as an injectable argument for tests:\n  1. `unix_socket_probe(socket_factory=socket.socket)`: bind, listen and connect an AF_UNIX socket in a fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory, then remove it.\n  2. `package_index_probe(runner=subprocess.run)`: write a minimal throwaway project (`pyproject.toml` with `build-backend = \"hatchling.build\"`) to a temp dir and run `sys.executable -m build --sdist --outdir <tmp>` on it with `timeout=300` and `PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1` in the child env (so a warm pip cache cannot answer for the network). This is the exact command and isolation path `tests/unit/test_build_provenance.py` uses.\n  3. `semgrep_validate_probe(runner=subprocess.run, which=shutil.which)`: when neither `opengrep` nor `semgrep` is on PATH it passes (those tests skip without an engine); otherwise it runs `<engine> --validate --config <one-rule temp file> --metrics=off` with `timeout=300`, `SEMGREP_SETTINGS_FILE` and `SEMGREP_LOG_FILE` pointed into the temp dir, as the detector backend does.\n  Each failed probe prints one line naming the capability and the error detail (no test lists, so the message cannot go stale), followed by one closing line: `make verify` needs these to give the same verdict as CI; run it where they are available (for an agent sandbox, outside it), see docs/local-dev-env.md. Exit 1 on any failure, 0 and no output otherwise. A probe that raises unexpectedly is reported as that capability failing, with the exception text. The probes are not retried: a transient network failure costs a re-run of a 10-second preflight, not of a 25-minute suite. The script imports nothing from `tests/` (scripts must not depend on the test tree), so it does not reuse `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.CapabilityProbe`.\n- `Makefile`: new `verify-host` target running the script. `verify` becomes `verify: verify-host` with the recipe `@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory lint typecheck import-convention test`, so the preflight strictly precedes the gates even under `make -j` or `-k` (a failed prerequisite means the recipe never starts), while the sub-make keeps today's parallelism for the rest. The `##` help text on the `verify` line gains \"host-capability preflight\". `make test` and its two pytest lines stay unchanged, so `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` is unaffected. No skip is added anywhere.\n- Docs: in `docs/local-dev-env.md`, a \"Where `make verify` can run\" subsection naming the 2 capabilities and the agent-sandbox case; correct the \"Sandboxed agent hosts without POSIX named semaphores\" subsection, whose claim that the counted-skip probes \"restore a real `make verify` verdict under the sandbox\" is no longer true (the shims stay for targeted pytest runs); update the `make verify` line in the command list (line ~547) and the \"stops at the failing prerequisite\" paragraph to include the preflight. In `AGENTS.md`, add `verify-host` to the `make verify` formula and one sentence pointing to the new subsection.\n- No config key, environment variable, or command-line flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/check_verify_host.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py` (new)\n- `Makefile`\n- `docs/local-dev-env.md`\n- `AGENTS.md`\n\n## Testing\n- `tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py`, all through the injected seams (no real network, no permission-bit tricks): each probe's pass path; AF_UNIX `PermissionError`; build runner returning exit 1 and raising `TimeoutExpired`; semgrep runner returning exit 2; no engine on PATH passes; `main()` with 2 failing probes prints both capability lines plus the closing line and exits 1; `main()` with all passing prints nothing and exits 0; a probe raising `RuntimeError` is reported as a failure, not a crash.\n- A test parses the Makefile and asserts `verify`'s only prerequisite is `verify-host` and its recipe runs `lint typecheck import-convention test`.\n- Manual, recorded on this ticket: inside the agent sandbox `make verify` exits 1 before `lint`, naming AF_UNIX sockets and network access; outside it `make verify-host` exits 0 silently.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Inside the agent sandbox, `make verify` stops before `lint` with a message naming the denied capabilities (AF_UNIX sockets and outbound HTTPS to the package index and semgrep.dev), recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Outside the sandbox, `make verify-host` exits 0 with no output, and the full `make verify` passes on the change (run unsandboxed through the operator's host-local verify-slot wrapper, which only caps concurrent runs and then calls `make verify`), recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_check_verify_host.py` covers each probe's pass and fail path, the exception path, and the Makefile ordering.\n- [ ] `docs/local-dev-env.md` and `AGENTS.md` state where `make verify` can run, and no doc still says the sandbox shims restore a real `make verify` verdict.\n- [ ] Gerrit gives Verified +1.","title":"make verify inside the agent sandbox cannot match CI: AF_UNIX sockets and outbound HTTPS are denied; refuse up front"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795207156392382001,"uuid":"ad9713d4-dc17-4383-bd3e-37cf9b699976"}